{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanA4TightSlice","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanA4TightSlice","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean4_tight_slice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean4_tight_slice","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanA4TightSlice.lean#L55-L65","doc":"**A=4 exact-order slice, PROVED.**  The A=4 slice of the general exact-order conjecture\n(`MilnorOrderLawGeneral §5`) holds: a nonzero leading coefficient `r = −3/2` and a cofactor\nwith `D_4 h = h^{2(4−1)}·cofactor h`, `cofactor 0 = r ≠ 0`.  Same shape as `borromean_tight_slice`\n(A=3); together they are the two proved points of the still-open `MilnorExactOrderConjecture`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean4_cofactor_ne_zero_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean4_cofactor_ne_zero_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanA4TightSlice.lean#L50-L53","doc":"The A=4 cofactor is nonzero at `h = 0` (`= −3/2`): the order is **exactly** 6, not an\naccidental higher vanishing — the lower bound `2(4−1)=6` is TIGHT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean4_deficit_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.borromean4_deficit_factor","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanA4TightSlice.lean#L40-L48","doc":"Trace-deficit closed form: `1 − τ_4 = h^{leadingOrder 4}·(−h⁴−5h²−6)/(h²+4) =\nh⁶·(−h⁴−5h²−6)/(h²+4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauL4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorOrderLawGeneral.tauL4","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanA4TightSlice.lean#L35-L38","doc":"The A=4 Brunnian `H₄` Markov-trace closed form in convention D (derived, not measured):\n`τ_4(h) = (h¹⁰ + 5h⁸ + 6h⁶ + h² + 4)/(h² + 4)`. Sibling of `tauBorromean`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}